  "body": "This is part of the effort described at\nhttps://github.com/w3c/mediacapture-main/issues/353. The spec text\nlargely parallels that for allowfullscreen.\n\n---\n\nDo not merge yet as it depends on some small updates to the mediacapture spec. It expects the current [allowed to access user media](https://w3c.github.io/mediacapture-main/#dfn-allowed-to-access-user-media) to become a \"user media enabled flag\", which exists on Documents instead of browsing contexts, and has an ID of `dfn-user-media-enabled-flag`. This is done to parallel Fullscreen's [fullscreen enabled flag](https://fullscreen.spec.whatwg.org/#fullscreen-enabled-flag). Of course also do not merge yet until the plan is signed off by the media capture spec editors, per https://github.com/w3c/mediacapture-main/issues/353.\n",
